The conjecture is true! Here is a proof.

Axiom 1 (eqNat_2): eqNat(zero, suc(X)) = false.
Axiom 2 (app_fn_id_nat_1): app_nat_nat(fn_id_nat, X) = X.
Axiom 6 (app_fn_case_Nat_nat_1): app_nat_nat(fn_case_Nat_nat(X, Y), zero) = X.
Axiom 7 (app_fn_case_Nat_nat_2): app_nat_nat(fn_case_Nat_nat(X, Y), suc(Z)) = app_nat_nat(Y, Z).
Axiom 8 (prop_twice_1): prop_twice(X, Y) = eqNat(app_nat_nat(X, app_nat_nat(X, Y)), app_nat_nat(X, Y)).

Goal 1 (prop_twice): prop_twice(X, Y) = false.
The goal is true when:
  X = fn_case_Nat_nat(suc(zero), fn_id_nat)
  Y = zero

Proof:
  prop_twice(fn_case_Nat_nat(suc(zero), fn_id_nat), zero)
= { by axiom 8 (prop_twice_1) }
  eqNat(app_nat_nat(fn_case_Nat_nat(suc(zero), fn_id_nat), app_nat_nat(fn_case_Nat_nat(suc(zero), fn_id_nat), zero)), app_nat_nat(fn_case_Nat_nat(suc(zero), fn_id_nat), zero))
= { by axiom 6 (app_fn_case_Nat_nat_1) }
  eqNat(app_nat_nat(fn_case_Nat_nat(suc(zero), fn_id_nat), suc(zero)), app_nat_nat(fn_case_Nat_nat(suc(zero), fn_id_nat), zero))
= { by axiom 6 (app_fn_case_Nat_nat_1) }
  eqNat(app_nat_nat(fn_case_Nat_nat(suc(zero), fn_id_nat), suc(zero)), suc(zero))
= { by axiom 7 (app_fn_case_Nat_nat_2) }
  eqNat(app_nat_nat(fn_id_nat, zero), suc(zero))
= { by axiom 2 (app_fn_id_nat_1) }
  eqNat(zero, suc(zero))
= { by axiom 1 (eqNat_2) }
  false

RESULT: Theorem (the conjecture is true).
